    "preamble": "Pintu Agarwala vs Unknown on 23 July, 2018 1 18 23.07.2018 Ab Court 28 C.R.M. 4881 of 2018 In Re : An application for bail under Section 439 of the Code of Criminal Procedure in connection with Karimpur P.S. Case No.103 of 2018 dated 12.6.2018 under Sections 272/273 420/120B of the Indian Penal Code read with Section 16 of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act And In the matter of : Pintu Agarwala ...Petitioner. Mr. Bhaskar Sen, Sr. Advocate, Mr. Atis Kr. Biswas ...for the Petitioner. Mr. Ranabir Roychoudhury, Mr. Mainak Gupta ...for the State.",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "It is submitted on behalf of the petitioner that he is in custody for 40 days and that the incriminating article has already been seized. Hence, further detention is not necessary in the facts of the case. Learned lawyer appearing for the State opposes the prayer for bail and submits that the report of the chemical examiner is awaited in the instant case.",
